  "description": "Alaska's lone U.S. House seat is being contested in 2026 using the state's top-four nonpartisan primary and ranked-choice general election. Incumbent Republican Nick Begich III, elected in 2024 after defeating Democratic incumbent Mary Peltola, faces a large field of challengers including Democratic pastor Matt Schultz, independent commercial fisherman and former superintendent Bill Hill, and several other candidates. Key issues in the race include the cost of living in Alaska, health care affordability, the influence of outside money in politics, and Begich's voting record on federal spending and tax policy. The outcome could affect the narrow partisan balance in the U.S. House.",
